{"availability":"available","full":"iluaii/fwm","name":"fwm","description":"Wayland compositor in C/wlroots where windows are physical objects (real Box2D rigid bodies) — and a full desktop besides: ten desktops on one scrolling world, tiling or floating per desktop, launcher, expo, screenshots, mixer and visualiser built in, live IPC. Legacy X11 version on the x11 branch.","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":175,"forks":5,"created":"2026-06-20T16:19:35Z","updated":"2026-10-08T11:32:15Z","license":"GPL-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fwm-website.vercel.app","topics":["box2d","c","compositor","desktop-environment","linux","physics","physics-engine","rice","tiling-window-manager","wayland","wayland-compositor","window-manager","wlroots","wm","x11","x11-wm"],"demo":"https://fwm-website.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.361Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.361Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.361Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.361Z","stars":175,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The name is physics window manager, with the ph spelled the short way. It has outgrown the second half of that — fwm is a compositor now, and not only a physics one — and kept the first.","A compositor written in C (wlroots) with its own built-in shell, ten desktops laid out on one continuous strip, and windows that are physical objects — mass, momentum, inertia and velocity, simulated by a real rigid-body engine (Box2D v3). Drag a window and throw it: it slides, bounces off walls, stacks under gravity, and comes to rest like a real object.","Physics is the first thing you see, not the whole of it. The strip is scrolled across rather than switched between, and each desktop on it chooses for itself whether it is a physics desktop, a BSP tiling one, or plain floating. The launcher, the desktop strip, screenshots, the wallpaper picker, the sound panel and the spectrum visualiser are built in, so there is no rofi, grim, slurp or cava to install alongside. Multiple monitors, layer-shell and session lock work the way you already expect, and so does XWayland. fwmctl reads the state, changes any setting live without touching your config…"],"features":["Real rigid-body simulation — powered by Box2D: impulse-based collisions, proper mass ratios, resting contact and sleeping. No hand-rolled solver artifacts.","Drag to throw — velocity is sampled over the last frames, a quick flick sends windows flying naturally.","Gravity modes — cycle Super+G between zero-g, space mode, and Earth gravity (9.8 m/s² at the compositor's 100 px/m scale). Windows fall, thud, and stack on the floor.","Realistic feel — dull heavy bounces (restitution 0.3), contact friction, no mid-air braking under gravity; long weighty glides in zero-g.","One speed limit, and walls that hold — nothing dynamic outruns maxthrowspeed, so a shove can never outrun the hardest deliberate throw and no window covers more than a fraction of its own width per step. Walls are swept…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iluaii/fwm/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9f1463699caa15eea7688092994303b2d22368e0e7327ae8c6373a072118878b","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.509Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.509Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The name is physics window manager, with the ph spelled the short way. It has outgrown the second half of that — fwm is a compositor now, and not only a physics one — and kept the first.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iluaii/fwm/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Grass along the bottom — an optional lawn on the bottom edge of every monitor, standing where that monitor's floor is, drawn as tapering blades shaded by how near the front they are. wind sets gusts travelling across it — 0 is a still lawn drawn once and left alone, 0.35 a breeze, past 1 a storm — and fps (24 by default) is the cost dial, since the whole strip is repainted…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iluaii/fwm/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9f1463699caa15eea7688092994303b2d22368e0e7327ae8c6373a072118878b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iluaii/fwm/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.512Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T11:32:15Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iluaii/fwm/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:21.517Z","hash":"9f1463699caa15eea7688092994303b2d22368e0e7327ae8c6373a072118878b","originalBytes":79379,"storedBytes":79379,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["window","desktop","one","fwm","windows","fwmctl","screen","where","rather","off","every","own","session","nothing","what","back","monitor","never","out","it.","which","strip","while","does","way","mode","same","gravity","how","when","compositor","config","docs","menu","physics","set","tiling","after","modes","wallpaper","without","camera","client","default","instead","move","only","them","tray","each","everything","over","per","two","any","because","output","there","cannot","goes","across","first","focus","keeps","layout","once","speed","still","takes","toggle","build","open","sound","through","true","drag","follows","fullscreen","mass","mouse","run","second","size","tile","along","bind","both","desktops","floating","itself","pill","pointer","click","comes","hand","key","launcher","name","socket","view","whole","action","anything","app","built-in","command","frame","hold","last","live","next","panel","see","sun","take","they","volume","whatever","x11","being","down","else","game","keybind","like","nested","new","other","put","reload","since","state","under","wayland","would","already","another","assets","bars","between","bottom","demo","file","focused","knob","real","rest","ring","runs","spin","stats","ten","throw","too","turns","visualiser","again","against","behind","binds","cava","change","cloc